Scripts trout can't run. Dialogs and DLLs stop a script from loading at
all, so it never half-runs; other unsupported things are listed, and the
rest of the script works.

-- bad.mrc --
dialog settings {
  title "Settings"
  size -1 -1 100 50
}
alias opts dialog -m settings settings
on *:TEXT:!sys:#:msg # $dll(sysinfo.dll,cpu,_)
-- good.mrc --
on *:NOSUCHEVENT:#:echo never
on *:TEXT:hi:#:msg # $window(@greet)
on *:SOCKREAD:sock:noop
menu nicklist {
  Whois:whois $$1
}
on *:TEXT:!q:#:msg # $?="Question?"
on *:TEXT:!ok:#:msg # still here
-- transcript --
! bad.mrc: line 1: dialogs aren't supported: they need Windows [fatal]
! bad.mrc: line 5: /dialog: dialogs aren't supported [fatal]
! bad.mrc: line 6: $dll: DLLs aren't supported [fatal]
! good.mrc: line 1: on NOSUCHEVENT isn't supported
! good.mrc: line 2: $window isn't supported yet
! good.mrc: line 3: on SOCKREAD isn't supported
me trout
chan #trout trout bob
active #trout
/opts
> /opts
< :carol!c@h JOIN #trout
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #trout :hi
= status: * $window isn't supported yet (line 2, good.mrc)
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #trout :!q
= status: * $?: input boxes only work in popups and typed commands (line 7, good.mrc)
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #trout :!ok
> /msg #trout still here
